+## High-complexity function
+
+`handle_request` in `src/request.cpp` is the dispatch switch of the server and the function the
+history touches most. It holds TP-C1. Its intended cyclomatic complexity is above 15 by the
+appsec-review counter (branches, loops, boolean operators and conditional expressions); the
+measured value is recorded in the guide.
+
+## Code-intelligence cases
+
+`src/synthetic.cpp` carries the appsec-review C/C++ graph-export fixture unchanged: virtual
+dispatch (`dispatch`), an unresolved indirect call (`run_callback`), two paths to one sink
+(`copy_unchecked`), a dominating and a non-dominating guard (`copy_checked`, `copy_unchecked`), a
+macro-mapped condition (`CHECK_LEN`), sign-changing conversions and an unclassified `send` sink.
+The fixed state of `read_asset` adds a `realpath` sanitizer and a dominating `strncmp` guard.
+
